PARITY NOTES (native reproduces the web source's data, composition, states and i18n)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web EnergyChargingPanel is a pure, prop-driven presentational panel (prop:
  chargingTelemetry: ChargingTelemetry | null | undefined). It owns NO data source and has exactly two
  render branches: a truthy chargingTelemetry -> the metric body; else -> <EmptyState>. The body is a
  GlassPanel with a cyan BatteryCharging header + "Energy & Charging" title above:
    - a 2-col MetricCard grid: Charger Voltage (fmtNumber, subtitle "V") and Charger Current (fmtNumber, "A");
    - a Charger Power row   : fmtWithUnit(charger_power_w, 'kW');
    - an Energy Added row   : fmtWithUnit(charge_energy_added_wh, 'kWh');
    - a Charging State chip : Charging -> cyan, Complete -> green, else -> gray; text = charging_state ?? Unknown;
    - a Battery Level row   : `${fmtNumber(battery_level)}%`;
    - a Charge Rate row (Zap): formatSpeed(range_added_meters_per_hour / 3600).

  Native reproduction:
    - EnergyChargingPanelProjection (the cached->projection adapter) reproduces the loading -> empty -> ready
      branch precedence, builds the two metric tiles + four label/value rows + the tri-state chip, routes every
      owned label through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade, and converts only at the display boundary (Charge Rate
      via the shared UnitFormatters.FormatSpeed; meters-per-hour / 3600 -> SI m/s -> the user's speed unit).
    - BUG-FOR-BUG (faithful to the web spec, the parity authority): the web formats charger_power_w (SI watts)
      with fmtWithUnit(value, 'kW') and charge_energy_added_wh (SI watt-hours) with fmtWithUnit(value, 'kWh').
      fmtWithUnit ONLY appends the label — it does NOT scale W->kW / Wh->kWh — so the web renders the raw SI
      magnitude beside a kilo-prefixed label (e.g. 7600 W -> "7,600.00 kW"; 5000 Wh -> "5,000.00 kWh"). The
      native projection reproduces that exact string rather than "correcting" it; the behaviour is asserted by
      Charger_power_renders_raw_watts_beside_a_kw_label_bug_for_bug and the kWh sibling test.
    - EnergyChargingPanel.cs (WinUI ContentControl) binds Model/Units (the web prop + parent loading flag) and
      re-renders on assignment, uses the shared TsGlassPanel, TsStatCard (the data-display tile that carries a
      value sub-line — the web MetricCard's subtitle maps onto it), TsEmptyState and TsSkeleton, design tokens
      for every colour/space/radius (cyan = TsChartSpeedBrush, green = TsChartBatteryBrush; never neon), the
      JetBrains-Mono token (TsTypeFontFamilyMono) for the row values, names the surface + each row as an
      Automation region, announces the loading skeleton as a live region, and emits view.opened on Loaded.
    - States: Loading (parent-supplied flag) / Empty (web : <EmptyState>) / Ready (web truthy branch) are all
      reproduced. The generic error / stale / offline branches are intentionally NOT present because the web
      source has none — it is presentational and prop-driven; the parent LiveTelemetryPanels owns the query
      lifecycle once for the whole live-telemetry section. This mirrors the established ChargerSpecsPanel /
      ResultPanel precedent ("no error/stale/offline state because the web source has none").
    - i18n: all 10 keys the web source feeds into t() already exist in apps/windows/Strings/{en,ar,he}/
      Resources.resw as translation.* with the exact English values (verified): telemetry.energyCharging,
      telemetry.chargerVoltage, telemetry.chargerCurrent, telemetry.chargerPower, telemetry.energyAdded,
      telemetry.chargingState, telemetry.batteryLevel, telemetry.chargeRate, telemetry.noChargingTelemetry,
      common.unknown. No catalog edit was needed. Unit symbols (V, A, kW, kWh, %) are emitted verbatim, exactly
      as the web source does (they are not translatable text).
    - Diagnostics (P1/S11): RecordViewOpened emits "view.opened slug=EnergyChargingPanel" and never a voltage,
      current, power, energy or battery figure (PII-safe; asserted).

